      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: This is my current workaround so unity only import it once with the proper format:\n\n1. Go to File > Build Settings... > Android\n\n2. Change Texture compression to ASTC\n\n3. Switch Platform",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-17T11:17:43.147Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "All is in the title, it's a total waste of time and ressources to change the default Android texture compression to ASTC AFTER switching the platform as it will trigger another (unecessary) full reimport of every textures.\n\nHow the SDK should behave:\n\n1. First change the texture compression of Android on ASTC\n\n2. Proceed Build platform switch.",
